   1
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/data.txt".
Write "sixteen bytes ok" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
open a file for reading called src at "vf_scratch/files/data.txt".
print src's size.
a number called 'the modification time' is src's modified.
If 'the modification time' is greater than 1700000000 then,
    print "modified is a plausible unix timestamp".
If src's size is greater than 1048576 then,
    print "File is larger than 1MB".
print "the size comparison did not fire".
Close src.
a text called 'the workspace' is "vf_scratch/files/fil-09-c1".
Create a directory called 'the workspace'.
a text called 'workbench path' is "{'the workspace'}/1example".
open a file called workbench for writing at 'workbench path'.
Write "mvqsqtdmmrodbyizwaprga5umfjdgq1cyy9oqx3tf4s4144g1q5dgbo3eimumuklkqqsdeeezl8jlarszhsbv3m2i1pcyuchjce93dkc9lu0ba7lc0u3kx1s2d44o7c63ogv7cenfcgkabqk0nho5jfaao5ynv4woi0xn54gw0tu9y2g0murxwrspy29j0n00g9e3yh19hn0o3g6oy1kychk1432n8dwyx8sybnndkqxtyjojh4wzmky8vfz1g62oa18b3ar9woxi4h09z77h" to workbench.
Close workbench.
open a file called workbench for reading at 'workbench path'.
If workbench's size is not 277 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected 277 got {workbench's size}", Exit 95. Print workbench's size.
If workbench's modified is less than 1 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected at least 1 got {workbench's modified}", Exit 95. If workbench's modified is greater than current time's unix then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected at most {current time's unix} got {workbench's modified}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-09 in range".
a boolean called 'workbench size guard fired' is false.
If workbench's size is greater than 0 then, Set 'workbench size guard fired' to true. Print 'workbench size guard fired'.
If 'workbench size guard fired' is false then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected 1 got {'workbench size guard fired'}", Exit 95. Print 'workbench size guard fired'.
Close workbench.
a text called 'the workspace' is "vf_scratch/files/fil-09-c2".
Create a directory called 'the workspace'.
a number called 'the gate' is 1.
If 'the gate' is 1 then,
  a text called 'the register path' is "{'the workspace'}/5example",
  open a file called 'the register' for writing at 'the register path',
  Write "lmy3u8hvfc22vw7i9z6t7ly8i4wq4fif" to 'the register',
  Close 'the register',
  open a file for reading called 'the register' at 'the register path',
  If 'the register's size is not 32 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected 32 got {'the register's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's size,
  If 'the register's modified is less than 1 then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected at least 1 got {'the register's modified}", Exit 95. If 'the register's modified is greater than current time's unix then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected at most {current time's unix} got {'the register's modified}", Exit 95. Print "FIL-09 in range",
  a boolean called 'the register size guard fired' is false,
  If 'the register's size is greater than 31 then, Set 'the register size guard fired' to true. Print 'the register size guard fired',
  If 'the register size guard fired' is false then, Print "ASSERT FIL-09: expected 1 got {'the register size guard fired'}", Exit 95. Print 'the register size guard fired',
  Close 'the register'.
